      <p>Akari stands out for its spatial, light-propagation mechanic — it's less about filling in numbers and more about understanding how light moves through a space. If you enjoy Sudoku but want something fresh, learning how to play Akari is a great next step.</p>

      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <details>
        <summary>Is Akari the same as Light Up?</summary>
        <p>Yes. "Akari" is the original Japanese name used by Nikoli, while "Light Up" is the English translation commonly used on Western puzzle sites. Both refer to the exact same puzzle with the same rules. When you search for how to play Akari or how to play Light Up, you'll find the same game.</p>
      </details>

